rops":{"className":"life-ad-layout life-ad-layout-toc"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-rail","data-dock-active":"false","style":{"top":"94px"}},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-dock","hidden":true},"children":[{"tag":"aside","props":{"className":"life-ad-space life-ad-space-sponsored life-ad-space-compact","data-ad-placement":"ad_dock","data-ad-group":"reading","data-ad-creative":"read_product","data-ad-ready":"false","aria-label":"Advertisement · Community recommendation"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-ad-dismiss","aria-label":"Close ad"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-x","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 6 6 18"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 6 12 12"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-brand"},"children":[{"tag":"img","props":{"src":"/sites/howtolivebetter/images/shengcai/logo.png","width":"565","height":"144","alt":"Official Shengcai Youshu logo","decoding":"async"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-copy"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-label"},"children":["Advertisement · Community recommendation"]},{"tag":"strong","props":{},"children":["Could what you know become a useful product?"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["From ebooks to small tools, explore how members spot needs and turn knowledge into something people can use."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-actions"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-link","href":"/en/shengcaiyoushu?sc_group=reading&sc_creative=read_product&sc_placement=ad_dock"},"children":["Explore the community and examples",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"18","height":"18","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-up-right","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M7 7h10v10"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M7 17 17 7"},"children":[]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"main","props":{"className":"life-reader life-tip-layout"},"children":[{"tag":"aside","props":{"className":"life-reader-sidebar life-tip-sidebar"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-back-link","href":"/en/book/19"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},"Back to index"]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-sidebar-caption"},"children":["While employed, upon leaving the job, and for work‑related injuries"]},{"tag":"div","props":{"data-ad-dock-host":"true"},"children":[]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"aria-label":"Chapter entries"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-01"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["01"]},"Overtime pay is calculated at three rates: 1.5×, 2×, and 3× the regular wage; failure to pay warrants a complaint to labor authorities, and non‑payment after the deadline incurs an additional penalty of 50%–100% of the owed amount"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-02"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["02"]},"Annual leave is calculated based on total years of service: 5, 10, or 15 days. If unused, employees receive 300% of their daily wage as compensation"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-03"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["03"]},"There is a legal limit on probation periods, wages must be at least 80% of the regular rate, and only one probation period may be set per employee"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"Calculating N: One month’s salary per full year of service; half a month for periods under six months"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"If a company fires you without 30 days’ notice, it must pay an extra month’s salary"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"When a company unlawfully terminates employment, the compensation equals twice the standard severance amount"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Never sign “voluntary resignation for personal reasons”; doing so forfeits your entitlements"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Save pay stubs, attendance records, employment contracts, social insurance documents, and chat logs before leaving your job"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/19-09","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Before taking up a post where there is dust, noise, or chemicals, check whether the contract mentions any occupational hazards; the employer must arrange and pay for three occupational health examinations"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Damage caused by dust, noise, and chemical toxins is irreversible: employers must provide protective gear, and workers can refuse unsafe tasks"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"If you’re injured at work or hit while commuting, the first step is to get a work‑injury determination; if your employer won’t file it, you must do it yourself"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Don’t believe the myth that “staying at work counts as a workplace injury”: if you suddenly feel unwell, call 120 first — don’t rush to clock in"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Even if the employer fails to enroll you in workers’ compensation insurance, you still qualify for full benefits paid entirely by the employer at the same rates"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"After injuries stabilize, undergo a work capacity assessment; disability grades translate directly into compensation"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"Three types of compensation for work-related deaths: funeral allowance, survivor’s pension, and one-time death benefit"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"If you’ve been bullied, insulted, or mistreated at work for a long time, don’t just endure it: document everything as evidence, then take action based on the nature of the abuse"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"When you leave a job, ask the employer for a termination certificate stating contract term, separation date, position, and years of service"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"Before spending severance pay, check individual income tax: amounts within three times the local prior-year average employee wage are tax-free; the excess is taxed separately, not merged into that year’s salary"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/19-19"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["19"]},"When moving to another city for work, transfer your pension and medical insurance to the new place of enrollment; contribution years keep adding up, so do not withdraw from pension insurance"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/19"},"children":["Chapter 19"," ·"," ","While employed, upon leaving the job, and for work‑related injuries"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"19-09"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["09"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Before taking up a post where there is dust, noise, or chemicals, check whether the contract mentions any occupational hazards; the employer must arrange and pay for three occupational health examinations"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["When you sign a contract, the employer must truthfully describe any occupational hazards associated with the job, how to protect yourself, and what benefits you’re entitled to — there can be no concealment or deception. If such information is omitted, you have the right to refuse the job, and the employer cannot fire you for that reason. The employer must also arrange and pay for three occupational health examinations: before starting work, during employment, and upon leaving the job. If the pre‑termination examination is not performed, the employer cannot terminate or end your contract."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost involved. When signing the contract, read every cl…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["According to the Law on the Prevention and Control of Occupational Diseases, when drafting a labor contract th…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Before taking up a post where there is dust, noise, or chemicals, check whether the contract mentions any occupational hazards; the employer must arrange and pay for three occupational health examinations"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost involved. When signing the contract, read every clause under “Disclosure of Occupational Disease Hazards” carefully. Make sure to keep a copy of each health examination report for yourself. The main difficulty lies in having to ask questions and request documents in person."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["According to the Law on the Prevention and Control of Occupational Diseases, when drafting a labor contract the employer must disclose four key points: what occupational hazards the job may bring, what health consequences might arise, how to protect yourself, and what benefits you’ll receive. The statutory wording is “the employer shall truthfully inform the worker and include this information in the contract, without any concealment or deception.” Should the employer later assign you tasks not mentioned in the contract that involve occupational hazards, it must again provide full disclosure and negotiate any contract amendments. Failure to comply gives you the right to refuse such work, and the employer may not terminate the contract on that basis. The three required health examinations must be paid for by the employer, and you must receive a written confirmation of this expense. Workers who have not undergone the pre‑employment examination may not be assigned to hazardous duties; likewise, those with specific medical contraindications must not be placed in jobs they cannot safely perform. If any work‑related health damage is detected, the worker must be transferred to a suitable position. Importantly, “an employer may not terminate or end a labor contract with a worker who has not undergone a pre‑termination occupational health examination.” Upon leaving the job, you have the right to obtain a free, certified copy of your occupational health records; the employer must provide this promptly. These records are essential for any subsequent occupational disease diagnosis, and they must be secured before you leave. Claims related to occupational disease are treated as work‑related injuries; details can be found starting at item 12."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["全国人大常委会 (2018). 职业病防治法（2018 年修正，第三十三、三十五、三十六条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.beijing.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengcefagui/qtwj/201711/t20171104_779851.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.beijing.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengcefagui/qtwj/201711/t20171104_779851.html"]},"（北京市人民政府转载）"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.beijing.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengcefagui/qtwj/201711/t20171104_779851.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["During an interview, asking just three questions can help you gauge whether a company is legitimate: whether the job involves occupational hazards, whether these are mentioned in the contract, and who pays for the pre‑employment health check. If the interviewer cannot answer or suggests “just start working first,” proceed with caution. The requirement for a pre‑termination health examination is a crucial safeguard — without it, the employer cannot end your contract. This examination also serves as key evidence for any future occupational disease claim; the same applies to the health records copy you must obtain before leaving. Claims for occupational disease are handled as work‑related injuries, and the corresponding benefits are outlined from item 12 onward."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link","href":"/en/tip/19-08"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Previous"]},"Save pay stubs, attendance records, employment contracts, social insurance documents, and chat logs before leaving your job"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link next","href":"/en/tip/19-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Next"]},"Damage caused by dust, noise, and chemical toxins is irre